# Orbit Student Information Architecture

Every student feature must answer **exactly one** of:

| Tab | Question |
|--|--|
| **Home** | What matters now? |
| **Learn** | What should I learn / do? |
| **Grow** | What can I explore / develop? |
| **Me** | Who am I becoming? |

## Hard rules

- Exactly **four** bottom destinations: Home, Learn, Grow, Me. Never add a fifth.
- Home is a **Today** briefing (Next · Priority · open Today · quiet Progress) — collapse completed; announcements live on the bell.
- **Learn** surface is only **Continue · Subjects · Upcoming**. No feature directory.
- A **Subject home** is the academic unit of depth (Topics · Homework · Assessments · Resources · Progress). Nested tools open from Subject or context — never from the Learn root as a menu.
- Filter homework/topics by subject params when coming from Subject.
- Homework, Classes, Assessments, Study AI, Paper Scan, Quiz live **inside Learn** (or contextual), never as bottom nav.
- **Ask Orbit** opens as a contextual sheet (`openAskOrbit`) — never an AI Dashboard tab.
- Competitions, clubs, challenges, workshops live in **Grow**. Cap visible interests at **4**. For You reasons must be honest (match or admit school-open default).
- **Me** is identity + growth (portfolio, achievements, interests). Attendance, progress reports, teachers live under **School records**.
- Settings (theme, language, sign out) live behind the Me gear — not in the global top bar.
- Fees stay out of student MVP.
- Information levels: **Glance → Understand · Explore**. Never put Level 3 detail on Home.
- Hide bottom nav on deep Level 3 stacks (`deepFocus`) for one-hand focus.
- If a feature does not fit a tab, rehome it — do not create new navigation.

## Build order

Stage 1 Home/Today → Stage 2 Learn shell → Stage 3 Learn→Do loop → Stage 4 contextual intelligence → Stage 5 Grow → Stage 6 Discover → Stage 7 Me → Stage 8 Portfolio.
